  {
    "id": "a8d77c3ee8f9c0072c54",
    "sourceHash": "a8d77c3ee8f9c0072c540bdb8eb985c47a10237b1b935a51456febae1e9c2c11",
    "th": "Between adventures: set_lifestyle when the party settles in town (each dawn there then costs every character their lifestyle; set none when they take to the road), and downtime for days of crafting, a profession, recuperating, research or training: the server moves the clock once, charges the costs, keeps the progress and grants what is finished. Never charge a lifestyle with modify_gold yourself. A character carries at most 15 x Strength pounds (the server refuses a grant or purchase past it and slows one already over it to 5 feet) and pushes, drags or lifts at most 30 x Strength pounds: shifting something heavy is lift, which says whether it moves. Putting armor on or taking it off outside a fight takes its SRD minutes, and the server moves the clock.",
    "status": "technical",
    "reviewed": true,
    "reason": "AI-only tool schema/name or internal prompt contract; not rendered to players. Preserve canonical English."
  },
